# Citation metadata for ETNA (Citation File Format 1.2.0, https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a GitHub
# release (once the repository is linked to Zenodo, issue #3 P1.3).
#
# `version` must equal etna/_version.py (checked by .github/workflows/matrix.yml).
# No DOI yet: one is minted by Zenodo for the first tagged release. Do not add a DOI,
# identifier or date-released by hand before it exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ETNA in your work, please cite the software using the metadata in this
  file (a DOI will be added once the first release is archived on Zenodo).
type: software
title: "ETNA: Epitaxial Tcad Numerical Analysis"
abstract: >-
  ETNA is a Python TCAD library with a Streamlit UI for 4H-SiC p+/n-/n+ radiation
  detectors (proton dosimetry and microdosimetry). It solves Poisson plus electron/hole
  drift-diffusion in 1D and 2D with devsim and two numba engines that reproduce devsim
  inside checked parameter boxes, and derives C-V, depletion and field profiles,
  charge-collection efficiency, dark current, radiation-damage, temperature, dose-rate
  and microdosimetric observables.
authors:
  - family-names: Scalia
    given-names: Cesare
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8399-6549"
version: 5.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ngcex/sic-tcad-detector"
url: "https://github.com/ngcex/sic-tcad-detector"
keywords:
  - TCAD
  - silicon carbide
  - 4H-SiC
  - drift-diffusion
  - radiation detectors
  - dosimetry
  - microdosimetry
  - devsim
  - numba

